 {"acceptance_criteria": "Battery detects at least one start command (python3 -m src.dashboard.main and/or python3 ram_map_server.py) and a web surface for this repo, then emits a non-vacuous ui-probe verdict plus non-vacuous chaos-corruption/-errorpath results; alternatively the detector gaps are documented and the project's surfaces registered with the battery so the cells stop reporting N/A/UNVERIFIED for a UI that answers 200. GATE ARM: re-run the battery with `bash ~/.hermes/scripts/bunker-qa.sh launch /home/kara/ai_plays_poke`; expect the ui-probe cell to print a non-vacuous verdict (not N/A) and the chaos-corruption and chaos-errorpath cells to run rather than print UNVERIFIED with no start command detected.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-18T03:09:42.431190Z", "detail": "Same tick/agent/HEAD (eeec1a8a8028e863b8847494a9425712447ab2dc). Cells: ui-probe=N/A ('no web UI detected'), chaos-corruption=UNVERIFIED and chaos-errorpath=INFO ('no start command detected - entrypoint not observable'). Reality: documented run surfaces exist - docs/api/dashboard.md:13 'python3 -m src.dashboard.main' (FastAPI, PTP_DASHBOARD_PORT default 8000), README:170 'python3 ram_map_server.py' (:8099 live RAM-map viewer), README:156-168 'web/index.html' browser live viewer. Reproduced myself on the clean agent: PTP_DASHBOARD_PORT=8123 ~/tools/venv/bin/python -m src.dashboard.main -> GET / = 200 with '<title>PTP-01X Observability Dashboard</title>', GET /health = 200, GET /metrics = 401 (auth required). So the battery's zero-UI and no-start-command conclusions are detector misses: the UI is never probed and restart/corruption behavior is never exercised. Same defect class as QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-18 (complete) whose 'chaos-disconnect + chaos-corruption cells vacuous' finding persists.", "foreman_note": "Recurrence of QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-18 (complete, 'chaos-disconnect + chaos-corruption cells vacuous'). Harness coverage row - no product defect inferred.", "id": "QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-18-R2"