 {"acceptance_criteria": "Upgrade cell resolves the project's distribution channel (GitHub Release wheel assets) and upgrades across two published tags, or records SKIPPED-with-reason stating that PyPI absence is intentional per RELEASE-006/RELEASE-012; no product defect is filed from the pip-index result alone. GATE ARM: re-run the battery's upgrade cell with `bash ~/.hermes/scripts/bunker-qa.sh launch /home/kara/ai_plays_poke`; expect the cell to resolve the GitHub Release wheel channel and print either a pass across two published tags or an explicit SKIPPED-with-reason, and cite the cell log path in worker_summary.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-18T03:09:42.431190Z", "detail": "Cell upgrade=FAIL: 'pip install ptp-01x-pokemon-ai==1.1.0' rc=1, 'from versions: none'. Confirmed the index really is empty: https://pypi.org/pypi/ptp-01x-pokemon-ai/json = 404 and test.pypi.org = 404. That absence is intentional distribution policy, not a defect: RELEASE-006 and RELEASE-012 (both complete) publish a tag plus a GitHub Release carrying wheel+sdist assets. gh release view v1.1.0/v1.2.0 shows ptp_01x_pokemon_ai-1.1.0-py3-none-any.whl (360028 B) and -1.2.0-py3-none-any.whl (360615 B) plus sdists. I verified the real upgrade path myself in a fresh venv from those assets: install 1.1.0 -> Version 1.1.0 with flattened top-level modules (core, dashboard, db, observability, ptp_cli, schemas, vision); pip install --upgrade 1.2.0 -> Version 1.2.0 with top-level 'src' only, i.e. the old flattened modules were removed by pip and do not shadow the new package (the RELEASE-007 defect does not resurrect on upgrade). Upgrade path = OK on the project's actual channel; only the cell's package-index assumption fails.", "foreman_note": "Tick ai-plays-poke-qa-2026-11-18-02-23-05. Overlaps QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-26 (pending, non-PEP440 probe tags break pip) but is a different defect: this is the cell's channel assumption, and the release-wheel upgrade was measured green.", "id": "QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-030", "priority": "P3", "reasoning": "Grading PyPI absence as an upgrade failure would be a false product defect. The row records the measured verdict (upgrade works from release wheels) and asks the battery to resolve the project's real distribution channel instead of assuming an index.", "source": "qa-bunker", "status": "pending", "title": "[P3] upgrade cell premise mismatch: it expects a PyPI artifact while this project ships wheels on GitHub Releases - release-wheel upgrade 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0 verified clean", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T06:21:43.711097Z", "deferred": true, "defer_reason": "ROUTED (foreman ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-11-18-13-57-02): the upgrade cell hard-codes a PyPI index premise; the remedy (resolve the project's real distribution channel: GitHub Release wheel assets per RELEASE-006/RELEASE-012) is a bunker-qa.sh cell change, not ai_plays_poke code. The measured verdict is already in the row: upgrade 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0 from release wheels is clean. Owner: qa-foreman / bunker-qa lane.", "defer_review_by": "2026-11-25"}
-{"acceptance_criteria": "1) Add a new pytest module under tests/ that walks every \"file:line\" code citation in docs/observability-spec.md and docs/api/cron_runner.md (skipping the dated audit-history bodies those pages declare as history) and asserts each cited line still contains the symbol named on the same doc line, or sits inside the function the doc names; name the new module file in worker_summary. 2) Proof: run `pytest tests/ -q`; expect exit 0 and the new module's test names printed in the output. 3) Negative proof: the module must FAIL when one citation is moved 20 lines in a scratch copy of the doc (do not commit the sabotage) — a guard that cannot bite is not a guard. 4) Runtime under 5s, no network, no LLM. 5) Test-only diff; `ruff check tests/` prints no findings.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-18T19:17:49.271447Z", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "521cafce89d4f8c0dc97490f06f80f1cb8cffa69f997fc93c2e27ecf5cf917f9"}, "foreman_note": null, "id": "DOC-028", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Tier-2 judge b5128a5b passed DOC-027 on merit but named one uncovered failure path: absolute line-number citations in docs/observability-spec.md and docs/api/cron_runner.md drift silently after any future edit to cron_runner.py or src/observability/metrics.py, because nothing in CI re-resolves them. DOC-027 needed three judge rounds to converge exactly because of such drift.", "source": null, "status": "pending", "title": "[DOC][P2] citation drift guard: nothing re-resolves doc line citations, so the DOC-027 fixes will silently rot", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T06:21:43.478612Z", "capability_tags": ["docs"], "type": "chore"}
