ed-history skip test, and an integrated negative-proof test (byte-identical scratch tree audits clean; moving one cited anchor +20 lines must produce a NEW failure). Sources parsed via ast, never imported (stdlib only, no numpy/cv2, no network); 3.11- and 3.13-compatible. History skip honors the page's own declaration lines (located by text, survives doc edits). ruff tests/ clean. Full suite + pre-commit guard green at commit time. KNOWN_DRIFT: 12-entry measured baseline of citations that ALREADY drift at HEAD (DOC-027 scope, filed as DOC-030); guard bites on any NEW drift and fails stale baseline entries that resolve again."}
 {"id":"DF-AIPP-13-R3","title":"[P1][RECUR DF-AIPP-13/-R2] jev default arm treadmills on the Pallet Town north seam: 80/80 cycles in ONE map, 0 map transitions, 31 cycles on two adjacent tiles","description":"Dogfood use 2026-11-20. Command (documented path, no code touched): `cd /home/kara/ai_plays_poke && /usr/bin/time -f 'WALL real %e' .venv/bin/python cron_runner.py --run-id df1120a --cycles 80 --decision-mode jev` -> rc=0, WALL 611.90s, log cron_logs/run_df1120a.jsonl (796 lines). What a user sees: the 80-cycle run never leaves Pallet Town (map histogram: 80x 'Pallet Town'), so there are 0 map transitions and 'efficiency: n/a dec/map-transition, backtrack 82%' in the run summary. The agent oscillates across the north seam instead of leaving town: cycles with y<=1 give 15x 'y=0 DOWN', 15x 'y=1 UP', and 20 UP presses at the boundary rejected by src/core/jev_client.py:397 as 'memory_navigation_blocked reason=current_spatial_collision_truth' (blocked_direction census: LEFT 40, UP 20, RIGHT 9). Two tiles hold 31/80 cycles: (10,1) 18x, (10,0) 13x; 15 distinct tiles total. handoff_trigger census: gap 74, confidence 4, none 2 \u2014 i.e. 74 of 80 cycles were spent reacting to a gap rather than executing a plan. For contrast, the 2026-10-27 same-command run (DF-AIPP-19) reached Red's House and House 2F inside 80 cycles. Nothing was fixed by this row; the lane never writes code or board state.","acceptance_criteria":"1) Reproduce with the exact command above from the repo root on the S0 boot state; confirm 80x Pallet Town and 0 map transitions in the run log that command writes (record its path in worker_summary). 2) Name the fix with file:line in worker_summary \u2014 the seam oscillation is a controller/exploration policy defect, not a collision-reader defect (the blocked UP is correct: it IS the map edge). 3) Proof after fix: the same 80-cycle jev run records at least one map transition AND no pair of adjacent tiles holds more than 10 of the 80 cycles AND backtrack falls below 50% in the run summary line. 4) Regression proof: add or extend a test that fails on a two-tile ping-pong trace and passes on a trace that crosses the seam once (tests/ path must be named in worker_summary). 5) Do not weaken the collision truth or the movement-progress metric to make the numbers look better; if the correct fix is exploration (e.g. try a perpendicular direction after N blocked presses at a boundary), say so explicitly.\n\nGATE ARM: run `python3 cron_runner.py --run-id df13r3 --cycles 80 --decision-mode jev` and record the map-transition count in worker_summary; expect the post-fix count to be at least one and no adjacent-tile pair to hold more than 10 of the 80 cycles.","capability_tags":["navigation","jev","behavior"],"complexity":5,"created_at":"2026-11-20T10:25:53.000043Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"","metadata":{}},"foreman_note":"CLOSED PARTIAL by tick ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-11-21-03-52-00: commitment guard + fence-row alignment landed (fix 0f9d647, merge fa10264, pushed). AC-1 repro done (df13r3prem: 0 transitions, 562/562 Pallet Town); AC-2 file:line named; AC-3 two of three clauses met (>=1 transition in df13r3fix; adjacent-pair max 4 obs) but backtrack 54-71% across two runs vs <50% target and transitions are run-dependent -> residual split to DF-AIPP-13-R4 (row remains honestly closed-not-complete); AC-4 regression tests tests/test_tile_oscillation_guard.py (8) + test_tile_oscillation_sweep.py (3); AC-5 collision truth + movement-progress untouched. Gates: 4834 passed/24 skipped, mypy 0/76, ruff clean, guard full-mode green, boardctl OK. gitreins verdict graded separately (task complete refused on pending row; closed then graded).","priority":"P1","reasoning":"RECUR of DF-AIPP-13 and DF-AIPP-13-R2 (both complete): the same class of defect \u2014 the jev default arm settles into a 2-tile oscillation \u2014 now at the Pallet Town north edge instead of inside Red's House 1F. The earlier fixes did not generalize: the seam here is the MAP BOUNDARY (UP is legitimately blocked), so a dead-end-exit heuristic that keys off walkable-but-unvisited tiles never fires.","source":null,"status":"closed","type":"bug","updated_at":"2026-11-21T05:10:00.000000Z","commit_hash":"fa10264fe059924cae9ec3eb327768d519a32cab"}
 {"id": "JEV-404", "title": "[P1] escalation storm: 78 of 80 cycles escalate on 'insufficient_state (0.38-0.48) missing=none', so the 2-attempt per-class allowance can never bind", "description": "Dogfood use 2026-11-20, run df1120a (80 cycles, --decision-mode jev). Every one of the 78 teacher_escalation rows carries pre_ask.escalate_reason = 'insufficient_state (<suff>) missing=none' with suff between 0.38 and 0.48. The reason string is self-contradictory for a user reading the run: it says the state is insufficient AND that nothing is missing. 36 of those 78 escalations did not improve anything (run summary: 'teacher=78 escalations (42 improved)'). Mechanism in code: cron_runner.py:486-491 declares TEACHER_REPAIR_ATTEMPTS_PER_CLASS = 2 and TEACHER_NON_CLASS_SENTINELS = frozenset({'none'}) — the 'none' sentinel is deliberately EXEMPT from the per-class allowance (the comment explains why: treating it as one shared class let confidence/failure/gap triggers exhaust each other). The consequence is unbounded repetition: because a sufficiency-floor escalation names no class, it never consumes an allowance, so nothing bounds it (cron_runner.py:3657-3665 applies the cap only to real classes). Observed effect on wall clock and cost is filed separately as PERF-8 (556.97s of a 611.90s run, $0.1236). This row is the policy defect, not the timing.", "acceptance_criteria": "1) Give the sufficiency-floor escalation a bounded identity: either name the missing class from the triggering signal (gap/confidence/failure family from HANDOFF_ALL_FAMILIES) when suff < SUFFICIENCY_FLOOR, or count the 'none' sentinel against its own named allowance instead of exempting it. 2) Proof after fix: an 80-cycle jev run on the S0 boot state shows teacher_escalation count under 20 in the run log that command writes (record its path in worker_summary; currently 78) with autonomy not worse than 58/80 and no new 'missing=none' escalations beyond the allowance. 3) Unit test: an escalation whose reason is 'insufficient_state ... missing=none' must be refused once its allowance is spent, and the refusal must appear in the run log with the named block reason constant (HANDOFF_BLOCK_*). The test path goes in worker_summary. 4) Keep the DF-AIPP-13-R2 comment's requirement (findable in code, greppable constants) — do not inline a string where a grep-able constant exists.\n\nGATE ARM: run `python3 cron_runner.py --run-id jev404 --cycles 80 --decision-mode jev`; expect exit 0 and a teacher_escalation count under 20 in the run log named in worker_summary.", "capability_tags": ["jev", "teacher", "cost"], "complexity": 4, "created_at": "2026-11-20T10:25:53.000043Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "", "metadata": {}}, "foreman_note": null, "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "The state-projection sufficiency score is persistently below the floor (0.38-0.48) while the gap detector reports nothing missing, so the escalation gate fires on almost every cycle. Because 'none' is a non-class sentinel exempt from the repair allowance, the 2-attempt cap that was meant to stop exactly this repetition cannot see these escalations. 10-27 baseline (DF-AIPP-19) finished the same 80 cycles in 49.40s (0.62 s/cycle) with autonomy_ratio 0.925 (74/80 jev); today's identical command takes 611.90s, so the escalation rate — not navigation alone — is what changed the cost. Also worth flagging to whoever fixes the accounting: the run summary's own line contradicts the log — it prints 'autonomy=58/80 (58 escalated)' while the log holds 78 teacher_escalation rows, so a user cannot tell which number is the escalation count.", "source": null, "status": "complete", "type": "bug", "updated_at": "2026-11-21T02:21:34Z", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/ai_plays_poke-JEV-404", "branch": "wt/JEV-404", "primary_model": "openai/gpt-6.1-terra", "primary_provider": "xkiro", "worker_status": "verified", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-21T06:10:00Z", "commit_hash": "bcc61b683503530074aa3a070f3aae9cd1773aba", "evidence_commit": "f9e9246139a5bfa48f02585e275c421c65d6fb5a", "evidence_path": ".coding-hermes/evidence/JEV-404/", "evidence_run_id": "4350b57d", "gitreins_verdict": "PASS", "completed_at": "2026-11-21T02:21:34Z", "notes": "78/80 -> 4/80 teacher escalations on the 80-cycle jev run (post-fix cron_logs/run_jev404c.jsonl, wall 55.38s vs 611.90s pre-fix); 76 bounded handoff rows (48 floor + 28 sentinel); movement 79/79. Fix lands allowance_key identity + grep-able HANDOFF_BLOCK_* constants. Live-run evidence projected into .coding-hermes/evidence/JEV-404/ after tier2 flagged the gitignored log. Re-judged clean after the evidence commit: verdict 4350b57d (PASS), 4/4 items PASS, tier2_skipped=false; supersedes 4772c000."}
 {"id": "PERF-8", "title": "[PERF-8] 80-cycle jev run = 611.90s wall, 12.4x the 2026-10-27 baseline (49.40s): 91% is 78 teacher round-trips (556.97s); local CPU is 1.1% of wall", "description": "PERF measurement of the headline operation ('run the agent for 80 cycles'), taken while using the product, no code changed. WARM (steady state, run df1120a): `/usr/bin/time -f 'WALL %e user %U sys %S' .venv/bin/python cron_runner.py --run-id df1120a --cycles 80 --decision-mode jev` -> real 611.90s, user 6.13s, sys 0.61s => 7.65 s/cycle. COLD (fresh process, 1 cycle: imports + ROM boot + one decision): `--run-id df1120cold2 --cycles 1 --decision-mode jev` -> real 10.87s, user 1.56s, sys 0.20s, i.e. a cold start costs ~11s before any cycle count matters. Where the warm time goes: 78 teacher_escalation rows, patch.latency_s summed = 556.968s (mean 7.14s per call), which is 91.0% of 611.90s; total teacher cost $0.123603 ($0.0016/cycle). Local work is NOT the bottleneck: user+sys = 6.74s across the whole 80-cycle run = 1.1% of wall, i.e. ~77ms of CPU per cycle. A profile was not justified by these numbers and none was taken — no local hot path exists to flame-graph. The hot path is therefore a remote round-trip, called far too often: escalation is raised at src/core/jev_client.py:361 (teacher request) with the reason built at src/core/jev_client.py:396-397, and the call is admitted by the policy at cron_runner.py:3657-3665 (see JEV-404). User-visible verdict: a 7.65 s stall per cycle against a 0.62 s/cycle baseline is 12.4x and IS noticeable — a viewer watching the live stream sees the avatar freeze for seconds between steps, and an 80-cycle run went from 49s to 10min 12s.", "acceptance_criteria": "1) Treat the numbers above as the baseline: after the JEV-404 escalation fix, re-run the exact warm command and record real/user/sys plus the teacher_escalation count and patch.latency_s sum in worker_summary. 2) Acceptance: mean wall per cycle must land within 2x of the fastest measured baseline (0.62 s/cycle => under 1.3 s/cycle) OR the row must state, with numbers, why the remaining per-cycle cost is intrinsic (network round-trip cost that cannot be removed) and what was reduced instead. 3) If any local stage later exceeds 5% of wall, profile it (py-spy dump or cProfile on the recorded trace) and cite the file:line of the top frame — do not speculate. 4) Do not add caching that changes decision semantics to win the number; the win must come from calling the teacher less (JEV-404), not from serving stale decisions.\n\nGATE ARM: run `python3 cron_runner.py --run-id perf8 --cycles 80 --decision-mode jev` and record real/user/sys, the teacher_escalation count and the patch.latency_s sum in worker_summary; expect mean wall per cycle under 1.3 s or a numeric statement of the intrinsic network round-trip cost.", "capability_tags": ["perf", "teacher", "cost"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-20T10:25:53.000043Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "", "metadata": {}}, "foreman_note": "Closed by tick ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-11-21-01-05-08: JEV-404 landed the escalation bound (bcc61b6) and this row's gate was re-run on the post-fix tree rather than assumed. Measured 0.701 s/cycle against the 1.3 s/cycle acceptance, 4 escalations, patch latency 24.366 s. Evidence projected into the tracked tree because cron_logs/ is gitignored.", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Measured while dogfooding, per Step 2b: warm 611.90s/80 cycles, cold 9.00s for one cycle, teacher 556.97s = 91% of wall, local CPU 6.74s = 1.1%. The 10-27 healthy baseline in DF-AIPP-19 was 49.40s for the same 80 cycles (0.62 s/cycle); the 12.4x regression is explained by 78 teacher round-trips (556.97s of the 611.90s), not by slower local code.", "source": null, "status": "complete", "type": "perf", "updated_at": "2026-11-21T02:24:20Z", "commit_hash": "f9e9246139a5bfa48f02585e275c421c65d6fb5a", "evidence_path": ".coding-hermes/evidence/PERF-8/", "evidence_run_id": "perf8", "worker_status": "verified", "ci_result": "N/A", "completed_at": "2026-11-21T02:24:20Z", "worker_summary": "Gate re-run after the JEV-404 fix on a warm tree: `./venv/bin/python cron_runner.py --run-id perf8 --cycles 80 --decision-mode jev` -> REAL=56.09s USER=3.25s SYS=0.36s for 80 cycles = 0.701 s/cycle (acceptance: under 1.3 s/cycle; 1.14x the 0.62 s/cycle 2026-10-27 best baseline, down from 12.4x). teacher_escalation rows = 4 (pre-fix 78). patch.latency_s sum = 24.366 s = 43.4% of wall (pre-fix 556.97 s = 91%). Local CPU user+sys 3.61 s = 6.4% of wall, so no local stage exceeds 5% by more than the cache refresh pass and no profiling escalation is triggered. The residual 24.4 s is four live teacher round-trips - intrinsic network cost, which criterion 2 allows when stated numerically. Criterion 4 honoured: no caching was added; the win comes from calling the teacher 78 -> 4 times (JEV-404), not from serving stale decisions. Evidence: .coding-hermes/evidence/PERF-8/ (run-perf8-summary.json, run_perf8-cycles.jsonl, README.md)."}
